INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(147700, 0, 1477, 0, 0, 0, 'The Temple of Atal''Hakkar', 'The Temple of Atal''Hakkar is the great shrine the Atal''ai trolls raised to their blood god Hakkar, the temple the green dragonflight drowned beneath the Pool of Tears. It did not fall to ruin under the water. Its halls still stand, ring upon ring, sinking level by level toward a deep round pit at the bottom, and the Atal''ai still hold the upper rings: warriors and witch doctors, priests and their slaves, and dead trolls of the tribe who have not stopped serving it. Below them the dragonkin of the green flight keep watch in the middle halls, and they have no welcome for anyone who comes in. The lowest halls lie flooded with ooze, where slimes, maggots and lurkers crawl through the muck. Explorers come for the trolls'' relics and for the secrets of the temple''s halls, others come to strike at the Atal''ai before their god returns, and a few come on errands for masters far away, after something only the temple holds.', 'tools/research/zones/temple_of_atalhakkar.txt (map 109: areas 1477 and 1417); reachable_areas.json lists 1477 only; WMOAreaTable root 1330 Az_Sunkentemple_Instance.wmo, root label The Temple of Atal''Hakkar; swamp_of_sorrows.json 800, 808 (the Atal''ai, the sinking beneath the Pool of Tears by the green flight), pointed to in one clause; DB spawns on map 109: Atal''ai Warrior 5256, Witch Doctor 5259, Corpse Eater 5270, Unliving Atal''ai 5267, Atal''ai Slave 8318 at z -54 (Hall of the Cursed); Atal''ai Deathwalker 5271, Priest 5269, High Priest 5273, Mummified Atal''ai 5263 at z -91; Nightmare Scalebane 5277, Wyrmkin 5280, Wanderer 5283, Whelp 8319 (faction 50, dragonkin) at z -91; Saturated Ooze 5228, Murk Worm 5226, Slime Maggot 8311, Deep Lurker 8384 at z -190 to -147; quests 3446, 3447 (Marvon: the circle of statues), 1475 (Atal''ai tablets), 8253, 8257 (Morphaz), 3528 (the avatar''s essence), 4146 (Atal''ai haze), named here only by kind'),
(147701, 1, 1477, 1, 0, 0, 'The Hall of the Cursed', 'The upper ring of the temple is the Hall of the Cursed, a chain of chambers circling the great well at its heart, and the Atal''ai hold it. Warriors stand watch in every chamber beside witch doctors who hurl lightning, hex their foes and heal their kin, and who run for help when the fight turns against them. Corpse eaters crouch among them, trolls who feed on the dead, and unliving Atal''ai, dead trolls still in the tribe''s service, fly into a frenzy when they are badly hurt. Slaves of the Atal''ai are kept in the chambers under their masters'' eyes.', 'WMOAreaTable root 1330: groups 5227-5234, 5238, 5243, 5257, 5258 labelled Hall of the Cursed; all eleven Atal''ai Warrior 5256 spawns at z -54 fall in them (wmoarea.py over every map 109 spawn); DB spawns at z -54 in the same chambers: Atal''ai Witch Doctor 5259, Atal''ai Corpse Eater 5270, Unliving Atal''ai 5267, Atal''ai Slave 8318 (no script) in small groups of warriors, doctors and slaves; smart_scripts 5256 (Strike, Rend), 5259 (Lightning Bolt, Chain Lightning, Hex, Healing Wave, flee for assist at 15 percent), 5267 (Frenzy and its emote at 30 percent; undead), base and module alike; creature 5256: 11 spawns, all on map 109'),
(147702, 1, 1477, 2, 0, 0, 'The Pit of Refuse', 'At the very bottom of the temple lies the Pit of Refuse, a deep round chamber whose floor is drowned in ooze. Saturated oozes heave through the muck and throw off smaller oozes as they fight, while murk worms, slime maggots and deep lurkers crawl the flooded floor and the passages around it. Around the rim of the pit rise six balconies, each holding a great serpent statue at its edge. Near the way into the room an ancient altar stands silent, and the serpents carved on it look much like the statues above.', 'WMOAreaTable root 1330: group 5261 The Pit of Refuse (x -536 to -400, y 27 to 168, z -190 to -91); all seven Saturated Ooze 5228 spawns fall in it, with Murk Worm 5226, Slime Maggot 8311 and Deep Lurker 8384 (these also in the Hall of Serpents around it); gameobjects 148830-148835 Atal''ai Statue (z -149, around the pit) and 148836 Altar of Hakkar (z -174), all in group 5261; npc_text 1923 (gossip_menu 1288 of the altar, shown to anyone: the altar stands near the entrance to the room; a large serpent-like statue on each balcony; they look like the ones on the altar); smart_scripts 5228 (Summon Oozelin: in combat in base, once at 50 percent in the module)'),
(147703, 1, 1477, 3, 0, 0, 'The Pit of Sacrifice', 'At the heart of the temple a great well drops through its middle halls, the Pit of Sacrifice. On its floor the dragonkin of the green flight keep their watch among whelps of their kind. Above them, on six ledges that overlook the pit, stand six champions of the Atal''ai, each alone on his own ledge. They are dead trolls who still fight for their tribe, and each is a power in his own right. Whatever the Atal''ai keep beyond the pit, these six stand watch over it.', 'WMOAreaTable root 1330: group 5211 The Pit of Sacrifice (x -547 to -379, y 9 to 181, z -100 to -11), the central well; the six at z -67 on its rim (Zolo -529,130; Gasher -528,59; Loro -467,24; Hukku -406,60; Zul''Lor -467,166; Mijan -406,131); Nightmare Scalebane 5277, Wanderer 5283, Wyrmkin 5280 and 24 of the 38 Nightmare Whelps 8319 on its floor at z -91; creature_template 5712-5717 (type 6 undead, faction 37 with the Atal''ai), single spawns on map 109; smart_scripts 5712-5717 (each: on death, set instance data 11); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Sunken_Temple notes (original version: six mobs on six ledges overlooking the Pit of Sacrifice)'),
(147704, 2, 1477, 1, 0, 0, 'Jammal''an the Prophet', 'Jammal''an the Prophet leads the Atal''ai from the Lair of the Chosen, the sanctum where the tribe''s deathwalkers, mummified dead and high priests keep watch, and he waits there with green power streaming about him. A shield of force barred the way to him while the six champions of the pit still stood. When the last of them fell he cried out to his people that the shield was down and called the Atal''ai to rise up. Ogom the Wretched, a dead troll, stands at the prophet''s side, and the whole lair answers when the prophet calls. Here he stands to defend the vision that drives his tribe.', 'creature 5710 single spawn on map 109 at -426,-86 in WMO group 5209 Lair of the Chosen, with Atal''ai Deathwalker 5271 x18, Mummified Atal''ai 5263 x6, Atal''ai High Priest 5273 x2, Atal''ai Priest 5269 and Ogom 5711; smart_scripts 5710 (Green Channeling on spawn and on reaching home); instance_sunken_temple.cpp SetData DATA_DEFENDER_KILLED (at the sixth: Jammal''an says group 0, forcefield 149431 opened); smart_scripts 5712-5717 set data 11 on death; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Sunken_Temple notes (killing all six removed the shield protecting Jammal''an); hinterlands.json 4723 (his prophecy and the exile), pointed to in one phrase'),
(147705, 1, 1477, 4, 0, 0, 'The Lair of the Chosen', 'The Lair of the Chosen is the holiest of the Atal''ai halls, the sanctum of their prophet in the middle reaches of the temple. Its keepers are the tribe''s dead and its priests. Atal''ai deathwalkers lay shadowy pain on their foes and send them fleeing in terror, and when one falls its spirit rises from the body to fight on. Mummified Atal''ai spread a fevered plague, priests and high priests heal their kin, wrap themselves in shields of shadow and call up skeletons to their side, and at the far end of the hall the prophet waits.', 'WMOAreaTable root 1330: group 5209 Lair of the Chosen (x -526 to -417, y -134 to -38, z -91); all eighteen Atal''ai Deathwalker 5271 spawns fall in it, with Mummified Atal''ai 5263 x6, Atal''ai Priest 5269, Atal''ai High Priest 5273 x2, Jammal''an 5710 and Ogom 5711 at its east end (x -426); smart_scripts 5271 (Shadow Word: Pain, Fear; on death Summon Atal''ai Deathwalker''s Spirit 8317), 5263 (Fevered Plague), 5269 (Heal, Shadow Bolt), 5273 (Renew, Heal, Shadow Bolt, Shadow Shield, Summon Atal''ai Skeleton), base and module; creature 5271: 18 spawns, all on map 109'),
(147706, 2, 1477, 2, 0, 0, 'The Shade of Eranikus', 'In the Chamber of the Dreamer lies the shade of Eranikus, a great dragon of the green flight. Near him stands a font, and the dragons Morphaz and Hazzas keep the passage that leads to him. While the prophet of the Atal''ai lived, the shade lay out of reach of every blade and spell, as if not wholly in this world. Only when the prophet fell did the dragon stir and become a foe that could be fought, and the green dragonkin of the temple answer to him.', 'creature 5709 single spawn at -658,-36 in WMO group 5260 Chamber of the Dreamer; gameobject 148512 Essence Font at -634,-52 in the same group; instance_sunken_temple.cpp OnCreatureCreate (5709 made not selectable) and OnUnitDeath (Jammal''an''s death removes the flag); creature 5719 Morphaz and 5722 Hazzas at -668,103 and -667,81 in group 5259, the passage north of the chamber; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Sunken_Temple (Hazzas and Morphaz guard the final boss through the southern hallway)'),
(147707, 3, 1477, 1, 0, 0, 'The Green Wardens', 'The middle halls of the temple belong to the dragonkin of the green flight, who hold the floor of the great pit and the passages around it. Scalebanes stand guard behind their shields, wanderers strike at the joints of their foes'' armor, wyrmkin spit acid and lull their enemies to sleep, and whelps of the flight swarm about the floor of the pit. They do not side with the Atal''ai, yet they turn on every outsider who comes down into their halls as fiercely as the trolls do.', 'creature_template 5277 Nightmare Scalebane, 5280 Nightmare Wyrmkin, 5283 Nightmare Wanderer, 8319 Nightmare Whelp (type 2 dragonkin, faction 50, the green dragonkin faction of Somnus and his kin), all spawns on map 109, at z -91 in and around the Pit of Sacrifice; smart_scripts 5277 (Improved Blocking), 5283 (Strike, Pierce Armor), 5280 (Acid Spit, Sleep); the module gives 5277, 5283 their spells and removes 8319''s AI (5280 untouched); faction 50 on 5709, 5719-5722 as well'),
(147708, 2, 1477, 3, 0, 0, 'The Avatar of Hakkar', 'The Avatar of Hakkar is the form in which the blood god can enter the world, and the Sanctum of the Fallen God, deep in the temple, is where it can be called forth. There the dead god can be stirred, and he will send his minions against whoever wakes him. His bloodkeepers carry Hakkari blood, and with it the eternal flames that hold Hakkar''s spirit can be doused. When every flame is out, the avatar enters the world, and there it must be faced and defeated.', 'quest 3528 description (the Sanctum of the Fallen God; invoke the egg''s power to stir the dead god; minions; bloodrinkers and their Hakkari blood; douse the eternal flames that hold Hakkar''s spirit; the avatar will enter our world; defeat him and place his essence in the egg); WMOAreaTable root 1330 group 5206 Sanctum of the Fallen God (x -526 to -408, y 228 to 324): Eternal Flames 148418-148421, Evil God Spell Focus 148422, the shade''s spawn point; creature 8443 has no spawn: summoned only by 8440, itself summoned only by the egg''s spell'),
(147709, 3, 1477, 2, 0, 0, 'The Circle of Statues', 'In the Sunken Temple the goblin Marvon Rivetseeker once stumbled through a great round room full of serpent statues, the room he remembers so dimly. He has become sure that the circle holds a secret, though the room is as dangerous as it is strange, and that the secret is worth the risk of finding it. Now he sends those bold enough back into the temple in his place, down to that room, to learn what its serpent statues and the altar among them are hiding.', 'quests 3446 and 3447 descriptions (Marvon, Tanaris; PrevQuestID 3444 each; QuestType 2, flags 0 and 8; AllowableRaces 0); tanaris.json 44024 (Marvon, his escape, his memory of the room on DONE 3444), pointed to in a phrase'),
(147710, 2, 1477, 4, 0, 0, 'Malfurion Stormrage', 'In the Chamber of the Dreamer the walls trembled, and Malfurion Stormrage appeared to the champion who had come in search of the green shard of the scepter. He knew why the champion had come and what they sought, and he warned that Eranikus would not give up the shard freely, for the dragon had been twisted by the same force the champion had set out to destroy. Even within the Dream, he said, an Old God''s power could reach.', 'instance_sunken_temple.cpp at_malfurion_stormrage (areatrigger 4016 at -662,4 on map 109, radius 20, in WMO group 5260 Chamber of the Dreamer: summons 15362 for a player who has 8555 rewarded and 8733 not rewarded); smart_scripts 15362 and 1536200 (on summon remove the questgiver flag, then say groups 0-4 and give the flag back); creature_text 15362 groups 0-2 (The walls of the chamber tremble. Something is happening...; Be steadfast, champion. I know why it is that you are here and I know what it is that you seek. Eranikus will not give up the shard freely. He has been twisted by the same force that you seek to destroy; Is it hard to believe that the power of an Old God could reach even inside the Dream?); quest 8733 (starter 15362, ender 15624; PrevQuestID 8555; QuestType 2, flags 64; AllowableRaces 0); moonglade.json 49316 (his warning recalled, the wisp, Remulos and the redemption on 8734-8736)');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(147703, 1, 0, 255, 'Zolo was the shaman of the six. He loosed lightning that leapt from one foe to the next and planted a totem from which skeletons of the Atal''ai rose to fight for him, until he fell on his ledge.', 'smart_scripts 5712 (Chain Lightning, Atal''ai Skeleton Totem), base and module'),
(147703, 2, 0, 255, 'Gasher fought with nothing but brute strength. He struck hard and often at whoever stood before him and gave no ground at all, until he was cut down on his ledge above the pit.', 'smart_scripts 5713 (Strike), base and module'),
(147703, 3, 0, 255, 'Loro bore a shield and trusted to it. He turned blows aside behind it and slammed it into the foe before him, until at last he fell on his ledge.', 'smart_scripts 5714 (Improved Blocking; Shield Slam on a casting victim in base, on a timer in the module)'),
(147703, 4, 0, 255, 'Hukku called on darker help. In the fight he summoned his guardians, a voidwalker, a succubus and an imp, and from among them he hurled bolts and volleys of shadow and laid a curse of blood on his foes, until he fell on his ledge.', 'smart_scripts 5715 (Hukku''s Guardians, Shadow Bolt, Shadow Bolt Volley, Curse of Blood; despawn of 8656-8658 on reset), base and module; creature_template 8656 Hukku''s Voidwalker, 8657 Hukku''s Succubus, 8658 Hukku''s Imp'),
(147703, 5, 0, 255, 'Zul''Lor swung a heavy blade that cleaved through those beside his target, and he wrapped his foes in frailty to sap their strength, until he was struck down on his ledge.', 'smart_scripts 5716 (Cleave, Frailty), base and module'),
(147703, 6, 0, 255, 'Mijan was the healer of the six. A mantle of thorns guarded him, and he raised healing wards and called up renewing light and waves of healing to keep himself and his kin standing, until he fell on his ledge.', 'smart_scripts 5717 (Thorns Aura, Renew on friends, Healing Ward; Healing Wave on himself in base, on friends in the module); creature_template_model 5717 display 6707, CreatureDisplayInfoExtra 4482: troll, male'),
(147704, 1, 0, 255, 'Jammal''an met his foes crying that the Soulflayer comes, and his lair came with him. He set totems that seized foes in the earth, called down pillars of flame and mended his people with waves of healing. Worst was his hex: he turned his foes'' own companions against them, crying Join us. Near the end he cried that Hakkar would live again. He fell all the same, and with him his hex was broken.', 'creature_text 5710 groups 0-4 (The shield be down! Rise up Atal''ai! Rise up!; Join us!; The Soulflayer comes!; Hakkar shall live again!); smart_scripts 5710, base and module (Earthgrab Totem, Flamestrike, Healing Wave, Hex of Jammal''an with say Join us; aggro: The Soulflayer comes and call for help in 90 yards; at 10 percent Hakkar shall live again; on death remove 12479 and 12480 and set instance data 1 to DONE); instance_sunken_temple.cpp spell_temple_of_atal_hakkar_hex_of_jammal_an_aura (when the hex ends while he lives and fights, cast 12480 and charm 12483 on the target)'),
(147704, 2, 0, 255, 'Ogom the Wretched, dead but still in the prophet''s service, fought at his side. He hurled bolts of shadow, sank a shadowy pain into his foes and laid a curse of weakness on them, until he was destroyed beside his master.', 'smart_scripts 5711 (Shadow Bolt, Shadow Word: Pain, Curse of Weakness); the module does not touch 5711; creature_template 5711 type 6 undead, single spawn at -426,-94 beside Jammal''an (-426,-86)'),
(147706, 1, 0, 255, 'Eranikus rose crying that this evil could not be allowed to enter this world, and he called his children to him. The dragonkin still alive in the temple came to his call. He shook the ground with stomps that staggered his foes, breathed acid over them and cast them into a deep slumber, until at last the shade fell in his chamber.', 'creature_text 5709 group 0 (This evil cannot be allowed to enter this world! Come my children!); smart_scripts 5709 (aggro: say 0 and set instance data 12; War Stomp, Deep Slumber, Acid Breath), base and module (module Acid Breath 12891 in place of 12884, Thrash at 10 percent); instance_sunken_temple.cpp SetData DATA_ERANIKUS_FIGHT (every living dragonkin spawn in a loaded grid set in combat with the zone)'),
(147707, 1, 0, 255, 'When the prophet of the Atal''ai fell, two drakes appeared in the Pit of Sacrifice, Dreamscythe and Weaver. Dreamscythe had a warning for those who had slain the prophet: they knew not what they did, and the dragons must destroy them for their own good. Then he came at them crying Turn back, do not wake the dreamer, beating his wings to hurl them back and breathing acid on them, until he fell.', 'creature_text 5721 groups 0-1 (Turn back! Do not wake the dreamer!; You know not what you do! We must destroy you for your own good.); smart_scripts 5721 (phase 2 until conditions 22/3: GetData(1) == DONE; then phase 1 and say 1; aggro say 0; Wing Flap, Acid Breath, call for help), base and module; creature 239020 Dreamscythe at -453,137 in group 5211, phaseMask 2'),
(147707, 2, 0, 255, 'Weaver, who came with Dreamscythe when the prophet died, fought at his side with the same weapons of his kind, battering his foes back with his wings and breathing acid over them, until he was brought down in the pit.', 'smart_scripts 5720 (phase 2 until Jammal''an''s death, then phase 1; Wing Flap, Acid Breath, call for help), base and module; creature 239021 Weaver at -459,128 in group 5211, phaseMask 2'),
(147707, 3, 0, 255, 'Morphaz, a green drake, kept watch over a passage in the far southern reaches of the temple. He called the dragonkin around him to his aid, drove his foes back with blows of his wings and breathed acid over them, until he was brought down at his post.', 'smart_scripts 5719 (Wing Flap, Acid Breath, call for help in 20 yards), base and module; creature 5719 single spawn at -668,103 in group 5259; quest 8253 description (Years ago, he overwhelmed me... ageless stomach) and 8257 (immune to all poison and disease), not told; azshara.json 1623 and 1627'),
(147707, 4, 0, 255, 'Hazzas shared the watch over the passage with Morphaz. He called his kin to his side, buffeted his foes with his wings and breathed acid over them, until he was brought down at his post.', 'smart_scripts 5722 (Wing Flap, Acid Breath, call for help in 20 yards), base and module; creature 5722 single spawn at -667,81 in group 5259'),
(147708, 1, 0, 255, 'When the rite began, the shade of Hakkar rose in the middle of the sanctum, and circles of summoning burned about it, spilling out minions of the god. Bloodkeepers came, and dragonkin of the green flight came crying out against the summoning and bent their magic on the shade to smother it. As each eternal flame was doused with Hakkari blood, the shade''s voice grew: it drew closer to the world, it tasted the blood of life, it was here. At the last it roared that Hakkar lives.', 'instance_sunken_temple.cpp spell_temple_of_atal_hakkar_awaken_the_soulflayer (summons Shade of Hakkar 8440 at -466,272); smart_scripts 8440 (summon eight Evil God Summoning Circles 148998; summon Hakkari Bloodkeeper 8438 and Nightmare Suppressor 8497 on timers; counter 1 at 1-4: say 0-3; at 4 cast Summon Hakkar, summon Avatar 8443 and despawn; counter 2 at 25: despawn and reset); smart_scripts 148998 (summon Hakkari Minion 8437), 8497 (say group 0, move to the shade, cast Suppression, add to counter 2), 148418-148421 Eternal Flame (on use, add to counter 1); creature_text 8440 (I DRAW CLOSER TO THE WORLD!; I TASTE THE BLOOD OF LIFE.; I AM HERE!; HAKKAR LIVES!), 8497 group 0 (No! We cannot allow you to summon Hakkar!; Stop! Infidels!, among others)'),
(147708, 2, 0, 255, 'Then the avatar came forth and fell on those who had called it, crying death to mortals. It lashed at those before it, laid a curse on their tongues that slowed their spells and drove one of them after another into madness, so that they turned on their own companions. For all that, the avatar was brought down in the sanctum, and the god''s shape in the world was broken.', 'creature_text 8443 (DIE MORTALS!); smart_scripts 8443 (spawn: remove flags, cast Avatar of Hakkar is summoned, attack; Lash, Curse of Tongues, Cause Insanity; on death set instance data 2 to DONE), base and module'),
(147709, 1, 0, 255, 'Marvon put his faith in the altar. Lying on the ledge after the trap that nearly killed him, he had looked down on it, and he believed it was the key. He handed over the stone circle and asked that it be brought to the altar of Hakkar.', 'quest 3446 description (I think that this altar is the secret; bring this token to the altar); item 10466 Atal''ai Stone Circle (3446''s source item)'),
(147709, 2, 0, 255, 'In the side of the altar was a hollow just the size of Marvon''s stone. Pushed into it, the stone circle locked into place with a sound, and the altar seemed to be waiting for whatever came next, as though it had more to show to anyone who studied it closely.', 'quest 3446 completion and reward texts (a depression in its side just the size of the token; it locks into place; perhaps you should examine this altar further); gameobject 148836 Altar of Hakkar, ender of 3446; gossip 1288 option (How could the altar and the statues be related) shown only once 3446 is rewarded (conditions 15/1288), opening npc_text 1935 and a script that lights six small lights in turn'),
(147709, 3, 0, 255, 'Marvon remembered more. From the main altar he had once set off a series of lights, one after another, and he believed that whoever understood what they meant could unlock what the room was hiding. He warned, though, that a great evil dwells in the temple, and that anything of value there would be fiercely guarded.', 'quest 3447 description (from the main altar I was able to activate a series of lights; uncover what these lights mean; great evil lies in the temple; anything valuable will be fervently guarded)'),
(147709, 4, 0, 255, 'The statues had to be woken in the right order. Each one touched in its turn lit up with a great light, while one touched out of turn lashed out with poison, dark energy or flame. When the sixth was lit, an idol of Hakkar rose in the middle of the pit, and with it its guardian, Atal''alarion, a towering troll who cried that his banishment was ended and the blood should flow.', 'smart_scripts 148830-148835 with conditions 22 (sourcegroup 1: in order, set instance data 10 and summon light 148937; sourcegroup 4: out of order, cast Atal''ai Poison 18949, Dark Energy 18948 or Flame of Hakkar 12354); instance_sunken_temple.cpp (at statue phase 6 summon Idol of Hakkar 148838 at -476,94,-190); smart_scripts 8580 (phase 2 until GetData(10) == 6, then phase 1 and say 0); creature_text 8580 group 0 (My banishment is ended! Let the blood flow!); creature 34521 at -480,97,-190, phaseMask 2; creature_template 8580 subname Guardian of the Idol, type 7'),
(147709, 5, 0, 255, 'Atal''alarion came on promising to feast on the bones of those who had woken him. He swept them aside with great slams and shook the floor of the pit beneath their feet, but he fell at last before the idol he was set to guard.', 'creature_text 8580 group 1 (I''ll feast on your bones!); smart_scripts 8580 (Sweeping Slam, Ground Tremor; on death clear the idol''s flags and set instance data 0 to DONE), base and module'),
(147709, 6, 0, 255, 'With the guardian dead, the idol could be studied. Its eye glittered brightly even in the half darkness of the temple, and it was clear enough to show something shining behind it. Slid aside, it gave up what the statue held: the treasure of the Atal''ai, the secret of the circle at last.', 'quest 3447 reward text (the eye of the idol glitters; something shiny behind it; the Atal''ai treasure is now yours); gameobject 148838 Idol of Hakkar, ender of 3447; gameobject_template_addon flags 4 (not selectable) until Atal''alarion''s death (smart_scripts 8580 action 104 and instance_sunken_temple.cpp OnGameObjectCreate)'),
(147710, 1, 0, 255, 'The way he gave was a hard one. Eranikus, now a tyrant of the Dream, longed to be brought into Azeroth, where he would stop at nothing to destroy Malfurion''s body, and yet only so could the shard be won. Malfurion called it a journey of redemption: the shard recovered and Eranikus cleansed of the Old Gods'' taint. He sent the champion to an agent waiting outside Darnassus, who would tell Tyrande without alerting Staghelm, and sighed over a fall from grace a thousand years in the making.', 'creature_text 15362 group 3 (Eranikus wants nothing more than to be brought to Azeroth from the Dream; he will stop at nothing to destroy my physical manifestation; the only way to recover the scepter shard) and group 4 (You will bring him back into this world); quest 8733 description (a journey of redemption; recover the green scepter shard; cleanse Eranikus of the taint placed upon him by the Old Gods; one of my agents outside the walls of Darnassus; inform Tyrande without alerting Staghelm; A fall from grace a thousand years in the making)');
